{
  "name": "polish-display-glyphs",
  "purpose": "iter-465 polish lane (docs/PLAYER_BUILD.md 7, docs/CUSTOM_FRONTEND.md 5.9, docs/INPUT_GLYPHS.md 7): ONE background PORT FEATURE roll (natural=false) proving (a) device-matched prompts live with a hot-swap keyboard -> DualShock 4 -> keyboard -> DualShock 4 -> keyboard on the title UI and the MAIN MENU (tools/glyphs/vpad_hotplug.py --plan polish runs beside it: ViGEm pads, so -Gates must carry SR_HARNESS_REAL_INPUT=1 and the roll must hold the game slot), (b) the DISPLAY OPTIONS page from SETTINGS: every row changed with LEFT/RIGHT and applied live (fps target, vsync, window size; display mode stored, the automated window stays windowed), RESOLUTION 2X -> RESTART NOW, (c) the relaunched child at the new scale, NEW GAME, the tutorial, then pause > OPTIONS in game (lane E L-c: the pause menu's own row; the DISPLAY tab's frame rate changed in gameplay, then discarded). Gates: SR_INSTANCE_ID=polish,SR_PORT_FEATURES=1,SR_HARNESS_REAL_INPUT=1; -TimeoutSeconds 1800.",
  "gates": "SR_KB_PAD_OBS=1,SR_PRESENT_DUMP=1,SR_PRESENT_DUMP_SPARSE_EVERY=30,SR_PRESENT_DUMP_SPARSE_CAP=2000,SR_HIGHFPS_PACE=1",
